  "summary": {
    "status": "DRAFT - not approved",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Ashcombe Garden Centres Ltd operates two garden centres with cafés, is based in Marlstone and was incorporated in May 2014. It is owned by its two directors, Helen Ashcombe (70%) and Daniel Reyes (30%), and employs 58 staff (52 at the last review). The company is requesting an increase in its overdraft limit from £120,000 to £160,000 to fund seasonal stock purchases.",
      "Revenue rose 5.0% to £2,940,000 in the year ended 31 March 2026 (previous year: £2,800,000). Operating profit rose to £180,000 from £150,000, and net profit after tax was £108,000. Gross margin improved to 44.0%, from 43.0% the previous year. Interest cover was 5.0x, unchanged from the previous year and above the covenant minimum of 3.0x.",
      "The facility is secured by a debenture over the company's assets and a personal guarantee from Daniel Reyes limited to £60,000. The current ratio was 1.30 (previous year: 1.40), above the covenant minimum of 1.15.",
      "Compared with last year's review, the differences flagged are higher stock, higher bank borrowing and no overdraft excesses in the past 12 months (one in the previous review period). No other material changes were identified. Stock rose to £402,000 from £318,000 while revenue grew 5.0%, which indicates that stock is selling through more quickly than last year. The existing overdraft is priced at base rate + 3.50% and is next due for review on 15 June 2026; the increase does not take effect until the Bank confirms credit approval."
    ],
